t;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/bbc/946950-commando"&gt;Game FAQs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Killer Gorilla on the BBC Micro</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/killer-gorilla-on-bbc-micro/</link><pubDate>Tue, 05 Jul 2016 12:18:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/killer-gorilla-on-bbc-micro/</guid><description>&lt;iframe allowfullscreen="" frameborder="0" height="344" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/FoHKu9Q-f1I" width="459"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Not a bad attempt after 20 odd years of not playing.</description></item><item><title>3d Printing the future</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/3d-printing-future/</link><pubDate>Wed, 05 Sep 2012 15:58:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/3d-printing-future/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 7 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="line-height: 0px; padding-bottom: 2px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://pinterest.com/pin/29273466299000502/" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="360" src="http://media-cache-ec6.pinterest.com/upload/29273466299000502_IZgiW3zv_c.jpg" width="600" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="float: left; padding-bottom: 0px; padding-top: 0px;"&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="color: #76838b; font-size: 10px;"&gt;&#10;Source: &lt;a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch/?v=qJuTM0Y7U1k" style="color: #76838b; font-size: 10px; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;youtube.com&lt;/a&gt; via &lt;a href="http://pinterest.com/alastair70/" style="color: #76838b; font-size: 10px; text-decoration: underline;" target="_blank"&gt;Alastair&lt;/a&gt; on &lt;a href="http://pinterest.com/" style="color: #76838b; text-decoration: underline;" target="_blank"&gt;Pinterest&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Video Tutorial of the dodge and burn tools</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/video-tutorial-of-dodge-and-burn-tools/</link><pubDate>Tue, 25 May 2010 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/video-tutorial-of-dodge-and-burn-tools/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 5 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 8 links are now broken — mostly deleted or made-private Flickr photos, dead Flickr &lt;code&gt;farmN&lt;/code&gt; subdomains, defunct feed-syndication infrastructure, and a since-removed YouTube video. Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OfDSWzIIVoM"&gt;Video tutorial of the dodge and burn tools&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Result is a bit over the top but he explains the use of the tools well.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Alastair Montgomery&amp;rsquo;s Photography&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://doodlem.blogspot.com/"&gt;Main Page&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="http://www.zazzle.com/doodle_m*"&gt;My Shop at Zazzle&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="http://sicklittlemonkey.deviantart.com/gallery/"&gt;DeviantArt Account&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="http://www.redbubble.com/people/Alastair"&gt;Red Bubble Account&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Converting MP4 files to other divX and mp3 formats</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/converting-mp4-files-to-other-divx-and/</link><pubDate>Wed, 20 Jan 2010 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/converting-mp4-files-to-other-divx-and/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I find myself often converting &lt;a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MPEG-4"&gt;MP4 video files&lt;/a&gt; to &lt;a href="http://www.divx.com/"&gt;divX&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MP3"&gt;mp3&lt;/a&gt; format to play on my &lt;a href="http://www.lge.com/products/model/detail/kc910.jhtml"&gt;LG phone&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;div&gt;I used to do this with &lt;a href="http://www.videolan.org/vlc/index.html"&gt;VLC&lt;/a&gt; application but this required too much button poking on my part.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;So after reading up on the Linux command line &lt;a href="http://ffmpeg.org/"&gt;ffmpeg&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="http://www.mplayerhq.hu/"&gt;mencoder&lt;/a&gt; utilities I&amp;rsquo;ve created this basic shell script to do it automatically. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;br /&gt;#!/bin/bash&lt;br /&gt;echo &amp;ldquo;MP4 Conversion&amp;rdquo;&lt;br /&gt;for f in *.mp4;&lt;br /&gt;do&lt;br /&gt; echo &amp;ldquo;&amp;hellip;Processing $f file&amp;hellip;&amp;quot;&lt;br /&gt; ffmpeg -i &amp;ldquo;$f&amp;rdquo; -vn -ac 2 -acodec libmp3lame -ab 128k &lt;code&gt;echo $f|cut -d. -f1&lt;/code&gt;.mp3 &amp;gt; /dev/null 2&amp;gt;&amp;amp;1&lt;br /&gt; mencoder &amp;ldquo;$f&amp;rdquo; -ovc lavc -lavcopts vcodec=mpeg4:vpass=1 -oac mp3lame -lameopts vbr=3 -o &lt;code&gt;echo $f|cut -d. -f1&lt;/code&gt;.divx &amp;gt; /dev/null 2&amp;gt;&amp;amp;1&lt;br /&gt;done&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;This will convert all the mp4 files in the local directory to both divx and mp3 format ready to be transferred to my phone. Obviously you need to have the ffmpeg, mencoder and lame mp3 encoder installed on your Linux machine for this too work.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Handbrake 0.94 transcodes DVDs even faster</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/handbrake-094-transcodes-dvds-even/</link><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2009 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/handbrake-094-transcodes-dvds-even/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 33 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 36 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Looks good :)&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="padding: 4px; background-color: #c3d9ff;"&gt;&lt;h3 style="margin:0px 3px;font-family:sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="font-family:sans-serif;overflow:auto;width:100%;margin: 0px 10px"&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0.25em 0 0 0"&gt;&lt;div class=""&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.pheedcontent.com/click.phdo?i=d65809a77240e869997c052c6e3d4068"&gt;Handbrake 0.94 transcodes DVDs even faster&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;div style="margin-bottom: 0.5em"&gt;via &lt;a href="http://www.downloadsquad.com/" class="f"&gt;Download Squad&lt;/a&gt; by Jay Hathaway on 11/25/09&lt;/div&gt; &lt;p&gt;Filed under: &lt;a href="http://www.downloadsquad.com/category/video/" rel="tag"&gt;Video&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.downloadsquad.com/category/windows/" rel="tag"&gt;Windows&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.downloadsquad.com/category/macintosh/" rel="tag"&gt;Macintosh&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.downloadsquad.com/category/linux/" rel="tag"&gt;Linux&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Eee PC Touch Demo</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/eee-pc-touch-demo/</link><pubDate>Tue, 20 Jan 2009 11:36:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/eee-pc-touch-demo/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;How cool does this look?&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;object height="344" width="425"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/5mvtU4xZPvQ&amp;amp;color1=0xb1b1b1&amp;amp;color2=0xcfcfcf&amp;amp;hl=en&amp;amp;feature=player_embedded&amp;amp;fs=1"&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true"&gt;&lt;embed src="http://www.youtube.com/v/5mvtU4xZPvQ&amp;amp;color1=0xb1b1b1&amp;amp;color2=0xcfcfcf&amp;amp;hl=en&amp;amp;feature=player_embedded&amp;amp;fs=1" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true" height="344" width="425"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-style: italic;"&gt;Having trouble figuring out how a touchscreen Eee PC could fit into your life? No worries, ASUS just did all the heavy synaptic lifting for you with the release of a near 6-minute video showing its new Eee PC Touch UI. A &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style="font-style: italic;" href="http://www.engadget.com/2009/01/06/eee-pc-t91-convertible-tablet-lives/"&gt;UI teased at CES&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="font-style: italic;"&gt; and built specifically for ASUS&amp;rsquo; new touchcreen Eees. All in all it makes a pretty case for why you should pick up a new &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style="font-style: italic;" href="http://www.engadget.com/2009/01/08/asus-eee-pc-t91-and-t101h-touchscreen-tablet-hands-on/"&gt;Eee PC T91 or T101H&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="font-style: italic;"&gt; convertible tablet later this year. Let&amp;rsquo;s just hope the processor can cope.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;Originally posted at &lt;a href="http://www.engadget.com/2009/01/20/video-sexy-eee-pc-touch-ui-demonstrated/"&gt;Engadget&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Spreadsheet Art</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/spreadsheet-art/</link><pubDate>Wed, 26 Nov 2008 08:36:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/spreadsheet-art/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This is a time-lapse video of three &lt;a href="http://www.geekologie.com/2008/08/man_proposes_using_google_eart.php" target="Bwindow"&gt;Google employees&lt;/a&gt; creating an 18,600 cell mosaic in a spreadsheet. As you will see, it has a nice&lt;a href="http://www.geekologie.com/2007/12/man_plays_jingle_bells_on_grap.php" target="Bwindow"&gt; wintry theme&lt;/a&gt;. Namely, snowflakes.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;object width="425" height="344"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/KpcgRlXe40k&amp;color1=0xb1b1b1&amp;color2=0xcfcfcf&amp;hl=en&amp;feature=player_embedded&amp;fs=1"&gt;&lt;/param&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true"&gt;&lt;/param&gt;&lt;embed src="http://www.youtube.com/v/KpcgRlXe40k&amp;color1=0xb1b1b1&amp;color2=0xcfcfcf&amp;hl=en&amp;feature=player_embedded&amp;fs=1" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true" width="425" height="344"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>What if the Matrix ran on Windows?</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/what-if-matrix-ran-on-windows/</link><pubDate>Mon, 17 Nov 2008 12:52:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/what-if-matrix-ran-on-windows/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;object type="application/x-shockwave-flash" data="http://www.collegehumor.com/moogaloop/moogaloop.swf?clip_id=1886349&amp;fullscreen=1" width="640" height="360" &gt;&lt;param name="allowfullscreen" value="true" /&gt;&lt;param name="AllowScriptAccess" value="true" /&gt;&lt;param name="movie" quality="best" value="http://www.collegehumor.com/moogaloop/moogaloop.swf?clip_id=1886349&amp;fullscreen=1" /&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;div style="padding:5px 0; text-align:center; width:640px;"&gt;See more &lt;a href="http://www.collegehumor.com/videos"&gt;funny videos&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="http://www.collegehumor.com/pictures"&gt;funny pictures&lt;/a&gt; at &lt;a href="http://www.collegehumor.com/"&gt;CollegeHumor&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>MagLev Toy Train</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/maglev-toy-train/</link><pubDate>Tue, 07 Oct 2008 08:15:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/maglev-toy-train/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;MagLev Toy Train, what you buy the geek who has everything for Christmas&lt;br /&gt;&lt;object width="425" height="344"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/5el1A5B-h3Q&amp;hl=en&amp;fs=1"&gt;&lt;/param&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true"&gt;&lt;/param&gt;&lt;embed src="http://www.youtube.com/v/5el1A5B-h3Q&amp;hl=en&amp;fs=1" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscr